WEBVTT

00:06.420 --> 00:08.230
It's been three years, huh?

00:11.890 --> 00:13.220
Damn that old hag...

00:14.240 --> 00:16.280
So she finally kicked the bucket.

00:19.320 --> 00:21.500
The place looks as shabby as ever.

00:24.550 --> 00:28.750
It'd be more profitable to tear the
place down than to sell it.

00:38.310 --> 00:39.450
Still...

00:40.010 --> 00:42.300
Where do I even get started?

00:46.100 --> 00:48.980
Ami-chan! You're done
with club practice already?

00:50.610 --> 00:56.490
I'm doing the laundry, so if you...
have anything, bring it... to...

00:56.490 --> 00:57.620
Huh?

00:57.870 --> 00:58.490
Huh?

01:05.460 --> 01:07.480
I'm home, Ouka-san!

01:07.960 --> 01:09.710
Club's over for the day!

01:09.710 --> 01:12.620
I'm soaked with sweat all the way
down to my underwear,

01:12.620 --> 01:17.210
so can you... wash... them... with...

01:20.560 --> 01:21.890
Wait, wait!

01:21.890 --> 01:23.240
What the hell?!

01:23.640 --> 01:26.890
Wh-Why are there two naked women in my house?!

01:29.960 --> 01:31.270
Make that three!

01:33.630 --> 01:35.050
No, four?!

01:38.760 --> 01:40.780
Who even sleeps like that?!

01:40.780 --> 01:44.040
Why are there five of them?!
That's too damn many!

01:46.520 --> 01:47.620
You!

01:48.450 --> 01:50.540
You're a burglar, aren't you?!

01:50.540 --> 01:51.130
Wai—

01:55.120 --> 01:56.100
Yah!

01:56.870 --> 01:59.970
Nice, Ami-chan! The karate club's paying off!

02:00.880 --> 02:03.890
It's said that there are goddesses

02:04.280 --> 02:07.900
living in an old coffee shop
on a beach somewhere.

02:16.760 --> 02:18.570
Come on in!

02:18.570 --> 02:21.350
Welcome to Café Terrace Familia!

02:38.050 --> 02:40.630
The Café Terrace and Its Goddesses

03:52.750 --> 03:56.790
Episode 1: "Familia"

03:53.120 --> 03:54.420
Sorry about that.

03:54.860 --> 03:56.790
Looks like we had the wrong idea.

03:57.910 --> 03:59.550
If you're really sorry...

04:00.580 --> 04:03.480
Then untie me and look me in
the face when you apologize!

04:03.480 --> 04:05.550
Hmph! You still saw us naked!

04:05.550 --> 04:08.310
Sorry I kicked you so hard.

04:08.640 --> 04:09.980
Ah?

04:09.980 --> 04:12.620
So you're Kasukabe Hayato-kun, then?

04:12.620 --> 04:14.620
Your grandma told us about you.

04:14.620 --> 04:17.580
She said she had a grandson
who got into Tokyo U.

04:17.580 --> 04:19.070
That's impressive!

04:19.070 --> 04:21.800
Forget that! Who the hell are you people?!

04:21.800 --> 04:23.950
And what are you doing in my house?

04:24.360 --> 04:26.700
What's your relationship with that old hag?

04:27.590 --> 04:28.890
Um...

04:28.890 --> 04:31.200
We're... her family.

04:33.510 --> 04:35.180
Uh, no, we're a family of two!

04:35.180 --> 04:37.960
Actually, it's down to
one now, and that's me!

04:38.550 --> 04:41.830
She told us to think of her as family.

04:42.340 --> 04:43.600
Huh?

04:43.600 --> 04:47.220
We've been working
part-time here since last year.

04:47.870 --> 04:52.390
She said we could live here,
since it had plenty of unused rooms.

04:52.390 --> 04:54.100
Devoted Member of Jouun Temple

05:00.060 --> 05:03.360
Which means we have the right to live here!

05:03.360 --> 05:05.320
What she said.

05:05.320 --> 05:07.740
Why don't you just go back to Tokyo already?

05:07.740 --> 05:10.870
"The right to live here"?
You're total strangers.

05:11.260 --> 05:14.620
In that case, I have the right
to kick you out of here.

05:15.480 --> 05:16.860
Who do you think you are?

05:16.860 --> 05:21.500
You left your grandma here on her own
for three whole years!

05:21.500 --> 05:24.590
We were the ones who paid for her funeral!

05:24.590 --> 05:26.040
Well...

05:26.940 --> 05:29.930
I got into a fight with her
before I started high school,

05:30.330 --> 05:34.570
so I didn't know she'd died
until the authorities called me.

05:32.430 --> 05:34.930
Devoted Member of Jouun Temple

05:35.310 --> 05:37.050
Poor Grandma!

05:37.050 --> 05:40.690
She'll never be able to pass on in peace
with a heartless grandson like you.

05:41.750 --> 05:44.800
I'll pay you back for the funeral.

05:44.800 --> 05:48.160
So just untie me already!

05:48.160 --> 05:49.950
Then get out of here!

05:50.850 --> 05:53.740
This is <i>my</i> house!

05:57.960 --> 06:00.920
Well, what do we do now?

06:01.380 --> 06:04.280
He's gonna try to kick us out.

06:05.160 --> 06:07.420
I don't know what we <i>can</i> do...

06:07.740 --> 06:11.390
I don't see why we can't just
ignore him and keep living there.

06:11.390 --> 06:13.310
I'm the one with rights here! Get out!

06:13.310 --> 06:15.930
I don't know about that.

06:16.280 --> 06:18.710
It's not really our house, after all.

06:20.840 --> 06:24.270
I'm having the house and the café
demolished to build a parking lot.

06:24.620 --> 06:26.520
I've already lined up someone to do it.

06:26.520 --> 06:29.530
This beach gets a lot of visitors
in summer, after all.

06:29.530 --> 06:32.200
Charging them to park might be good business.

06:32.590 --> 06:34.080
He's obsessed with money!

06:34.510 --> 06:37.750
Is he really that sweet old lady's grandson?!

06:37.750 --> 06:40.810
Cut that out. People are looking at us.

06:41.900 --> 06:45.200
It would suck to be told
we have to leave right away.

06:45.200 --> 06:47.590
Tickets for our concert
haven't really moved yet.

06:47.590 --> 06:51.960
And I don't have the money to move!

06:51.960 --> 06:54.600
I mean, I'm already struggling
with day-to-day funds!

06:54.990 --> 06:57.400
What should we do?

06:58.520 --> 07:00.680
What is it, Ami-san?

07:02.600 --> 07:08.490
I was too focused on stopping him when
I thought he was a burglar to notice,

07:09.350 --> 07:11.290
but now that I think about it...

07:12.360 --> 07:14.970
I'm the only one he saw totally naked!

07:14.970 --> 07:17.720
And I gave him a full-frontal view
with that roundhouse kick!

07:17.720 --> 07:18.540
<i>Now</i> you realize?!

07:18.860 --> 07:21.170
And he saw me changing...

07:21.170 --> 07:23.260
Well, he saw me, too!

07:24.840 --> 07:26.270
Now that I think about it...

07:26.270 --> 07:28.840
With five girls as cute as us...

07:29.200 --> 07:30.960
Well, there are always options.

07:30.960 --> 07:31.680
Huh?

07:31.680 --> 07:33.450
No matter how tough they act,

07:33.450 --> 07:36.830
guys have pervy stuff
on their minds all the time.

07:36.830 --> 07:38.190
They're nothing but apes.

07:38.190 --> 07:39.680
Ook, ook!

07:39.980 --> 07:42.860
Damn it... What's with them?

07:42.860 --> 07:45.690
Is that any way to treat
the owner of this house?

07:45.690 --> 07:49.050
Well, in any case,
I <i>will</i> kick them out of here.

07:49.050 --> 07:52.200
This is my house... after all...

07:54.840 --> 07:58.950
Stupid old hag! I'm never
coming back to this shabby house!

07:58.950 --> 08:01.340
Oh, really? Have it your way.

08:03.460 --> 08:06.420
What were we even arguing about, anyway?

08:08.460 --> 08:10.460
Hey, um...

08:10.460 --> 08:13.260
I was thinking about making dinner.

08:13.260 --> 08:15.580
Would you like to eat with us...

08:16.800 --> 08:19.050
M-Master?

08:20.950 --> 08:21.980
Huh?

08:25.560 --> 08:28.780
We'll start with a light jab in the
form of Ouka-chan in maid garb.

08:28.780 --> 08:30.620
M-Me?!

08:30.620 --> 08:34.620
That'll tell us just how much
of a virgin loser he is.

08:35.360 --> 08:37.240
We're counting on you, Ouka-chan.

08:41.360 --> 08:45.370
Just so you know, sucking up to me
won't change my mind.

08:46.500 --> 08:49.880
Oh, come on! That's not what this is!

08:49.880 --> 08:54.430
Also, do you always dress
like that to make dinner?

08:54.430 --> 08:55.800
Like hel—

08:57.320 --> 08:59.970
O-Of course I don't!

09:00.280 --> 09:04.670
I wanted to put in
my best effort for you, Master!

09:04.670 --> 09:08.610
Okay, fine. If you're gonna
cook it, I'll pay you.

09:08.610 --> 09:10.990
Okay, I'll make pilaf—

09:10.990 --> 09:11.910
Fried chicken.

09:13.200 --> 09:15.680
Huh? But pilaf is all I know how to—

09:15.680 --> 09:16.570
Fried chicken.

09:21.630 --> 09:24.290
I burned it just a tiny bit, but...

09:25.760 --> 09:29.850
Fried chicken costs about 50 yen to make
three pieces, so 200 yen to make twelve.

09:26.710 --> 09:29.920
50 yen x 4 = 200 yen

09:29.850 --> 09:34.340
Assume a restaurant sells six for 600 yen,
then double that to get 1,200 yen.

09:30.090 --> 09:34.090
600 yen x 2 = 1,200 yen

09:34.340 --> 09:38.430
1,200 yen - 200 yen = 1,000 yen

09:34.650 --> 09:36.340
That's 1,000 yen worth of profit,

09:36.620 --> 09:39.850
which you just spent an hour
throwing into the gutter.

09:41.160 --> 09:45.850
Riho-san! I didn't get any of that,
but I think he was just really mean to me!

09:46.140 --> 09:50.570
I see. So you're more than just
a late-blooming virgin loser.

09:50.570 --> 09:52.360
Okay. Ami-chan, you're next.

09:52.360 --> 09:53.240
Right!

09:54.380 --> 09:56.070
Join me on an evening run

09:56.510 --> 09:58.570
to strengthen our relationship,

09:58.570 --> 10:00.070
Hayacchi!

10:00.770 --> 10:02.140
"Hayacchi"?

10:02.140 --> 10:05.700
Yes! "Hayacchi" because you're "Hayato"!
It works, right?!

10:06.080 --> 10:08.810
Never call me that again.

10:09.670 --> 10:14.270
Also, are you really going outside
dressed like that?

10:14.270 --> 10:15.000
Huh?

10:17.520 --> 10:21.180
I can't! No way, no way, no way!

10:22.900 --> 10:24.300
It's black as night!

10:24.300 --> 10:27.060
Well, chicken has to be thoroughly cooked!

10:26.150 --> 10:28.090
You made a delicious meal.

10:28.610 --> 10:29.310
Yeah, but...

10:29.740 --> 10:31.560
This one looks okay.

10:34.360 --> 10:36.070
Ugh, bitter!

10:36.400 --> 10:37.640
Yeah, no kidding.

10:37.640 --> 10:41.070
What the heck are you wearing,
anyway, Ouka-chan? It's hilarious!

10:41.070 --> 10:44.330
What?! You're the one
who told me to wear this!

10:44.330 --> 10:47.330
It looks great on you. You look adorable!

10:47.680 --> 10:49.880
Yeah! Super cute!

10:49.880 --> 10:52.340
Why'd you have to make
that sound so offhanded?!

10:53.780 --> 10:57.480
Master dear, the bath is ready.

10:57.480 --> 10:59.110
Please help yourself.

11:00.470 --> 11:02.220
Ami

11:04.600 --> 11:08.230
I promise I'll get into Tokyo U, Grandma!

11:09.110 --> 11:12.230
Then I'll get a good job, get rich,

11:12.520 --> 11:15.480
and work some dumb shitbags to the bone!

11:15.850 --> 11:18.490
Stop talking nonsense.

11:18.490 --> 11:22.730
I think people who do things
like that are the shitbags.

11:23.620 --> 11:25.950
What? Why?

11:25.950 --> 11:28.170
Don't you want to be rich?

11:28.870 --> 11:32.220
Just a little money is all I need.

11:33.790 --> 11:38.390
Why'd I have to run my mouth
like some two-bit side character?

11:40.900 --> 11:42.630
Something's weird.

11:44.140 --> 11:48.380
Master, allow us to wash your back.

11:49.640 --> 11:54.820
And here I was sure they'd try a
stupid honey trap like that...

12:01.080 --> 12:02.920
The door to the café's open.

12:07.280 --> 12:08.760
Hey, anyone here?

12:14.520 --> 12:16.630
Hey! What are you doing?!

12:16.920 --> 12:18.880
Smoking isn't allowed in this café!

12:21.290 --> 12:22.660
Want one?

12:24.090 --> 12:27.600
Chocolate

12:24.790 --> 12:26.330
They're chocolate, though.

12:26.330 --> 12:27.210
Huh?

12:27.880 --> 12:31.220
I come in here to write songs for my band.

12:31.680 --> 12:34.060
It's quiet, so I can focus.

12:34.850 --> 12:37.870
Anyway, no smoking allowed
in a shop you're shutting down?

12:37.870 --> 12:39.570
Very upright of you.

12:45.540 --> 12:46.820
Aw...

12:48.080 --> 12:50.040
That was a pretty cute expression.

12:53.760 --> 12:58.970
I bet he dropped his guard
after that uneventful bath.

13:01.710 --> 13:04.470
This is the one trick
I didn't want to resort to...

13:04.990 --> 13:08.470
But we can't afford to hold back anymore.

13:14.640 --> 13:15.980
I never let you go

13:15.980 --> 13:19.460
to college drinking parties
because it's too dangerous...

13:20.230 --> 13:24.240
Sorry, though. Go be our
sacrificial lamb, Kiku-chan.

13:33.080 --> 13:36.300
It smells like a man in here!

13:37.710 --> 13:40.330
H-Hey, what are you doing here?

13:40.330 --> 13:42.380
What's this?

13:42.380 --> 13:43.550
Whoa, wha—

13:45.270 --> 13:48.470
You don't have much of a smell
yourself, though, Hayato-kun.

13:49.380 --> 13:51.440
You reek of booze!

13:51.440 --> 13:55.600
Rats. You just had to go and take that bath.

13:56.230 --> 13:57.940
Well, no matter.

13:58.680 --> 14:04.360
I'm sure working up a good sweat
will bring that musk back!

14:05.160 --> 14:07.110
Hey, you idiot! Stop!

14:07.750 --> 14:11.120
Give Kiku-chan just
the tiniest bit of liquor,

14:11.120 --> 14:14.120
and she turns into a shameless lecher.

14:15.510 --> 14:19.750
And one with an extreme smell fetish to boot!

14:20.260 --> 14:24.250
Time to show us your true colors,
Kasukabe Hayato!

14:25.040 --> 14:30.970
I've been into you
for a long time, Hayato-kun.

14:30.970 --> 14:32.390
Y-You liar!

14:32.390 --> 14:34.890
We just met today!

14:35.960 --> 14:40.900
There's no man alive who can
turn down those giant boobs.

14:41.960 --> 14:46.400
I'll capture the moment
you get excited on video,

14:46.400 --> 14:50.070
and I'll blackmail you with it
to make sure you can't kick us out...

14:51.520 --> 14:52.410
Huh?

14:52.720 --> 14:55.560
Hayato-kun...

14:59.110 --> 15:00.420
What are you doing,

15:00.810 --> 15:02.010
Hayacchi?!

15:02.420 --> 15:05.170
Whoa, hang on! I didn't do anything!

15:05.170 --> 15:06.580
Shut up!

15:08.920 --> 15:12.480
Wait, Ami-chan!
Do you realize what you're doing?!

15:12.480 --> 15:15.510
World peace, and all the girls in this house,

15:15.930 --> 15:17.550
are under my protection!

15:17.550 --> 15:19.940
You idiot!

15:22.690 --> 15:24.310
What is this?

15:25.040 --> 15:28.070
What does it look like? It's breakfast!

15:28.350 --> 15:31.270
Shiragiku-san made it,
so it's fine this time!

15:31.970 --> 15:33.070
Oh, come on.

15:33.600 --> 15:37.100
It might not be as good as Grandma's cooking,

15:37.100 --> 15:38.580
but I hope you like it.

15:39.430 --> 15:42.080
You don't... remember?

15:42.430 --> 15:45.090
Huh? Remember what?

15:45.090 --> 15:47.910
Nothing. If you don't remember,
it doesn't matter.

15:48.360 --> 15:50.340
Oh, yeah! Hayacchi!

15:50.730 --> 15:54.970
Sorry for ruining that
perfect plan last night!

15:56.720 --> 15:59.470
Am I the one you should be apologizing to?

16:00.610 --> 16:02.970
Riho-san already chewed me out for it!

16:03.870 --> 16:06.860
Don't tell me.
You're not too bright, are you?

16:06.860 --> 16:07.860
Huh?

16:07.860 --> 16:09.570
Well, kinda!

16:10.580 --> 16:12.170
Wait, what?!

16:14.520 --> 16:17.180
Who could that be, so early in the morning?

16:21.940 --> 16:24.810
This place is pretty big.

16:24.810 --> 16:27.580
We'll probably need two machines.

16:27.580 --> 16:30.600
You want to demolish the café as well, right?

16:31.120 --> 16:31.940
Yes.

16:32.470 --> 16:36.470
Then we'll need you to show us that
after we take a look upstairs.

16:36.470 --> 16:37.510
All right.

16:36.830 --> 16:39.930
They're really going to
tear the house down...

16:39.930 --> 16:41.470
Looks like it.

16:43.490 --> 16:46.460
Looks like it'll come to around this much.

16:46.460 --> 16:49.900
I'll be in touch as soon as we have
a more specific estimate.

16:49.900 --> 16:51.500
I appreciate it.

16:51.860 --> 16:54.480
It's up to us to stand firm now!

16:54.480 --> 16:57.950
Kill him and bury him somewhere, Ami-chan!

16:57.950 --> 17:00.420
Right. It's our only choice.

17:01.200 --> 17:04.440
Come on. Stop being ridiculous, you two.

17:04.870 --> 17:09.130
I'd say you're right to give up
on this place, though.

17:09.810 --> 17:13.880
A parking lot is gonna be way more
profitable than a coffee shop.

17:15.000 --> 17:17.500
Huh? It's... kinda loose...

17:18.470 --> 17:19.760
Oh, crap!

17:21.190 --> 17:22.660
The store sign...

17:23.020 --> 17:25.120
Hey, what do you think you're doing?

17:25.120 --> 17:26.770
S-Sorry about that.

17:31.360 --> 17:32.920
There, it's done.

17:33.840 --> 17:36.650
Now we can open up the café tomorrow.

17:37.460 --> 17:40.530
What does it say? Is that English?

17:40.530 --> 17:42.410
It says "familia."

17:42.410 --> 17:45.160
That's Spanish for "family."

17:45.160 --> 17:49.480
All of our customers at this café
will be our familia,

17:49.480 --> 17:52.620
meaning they'll be part of
the Kasukabe family.

17:52.620 --> 17:54.040
Family?

17:55.910 --> 17:57.020
Family...

17:58.190 --> 18:00.550
But hey, we're tearing it down anyway.

18:01.230 --> 18:05.080
It's fine, right? I'll go ahead
and scrap this for you.

18:05.940 --> 18:06.810
Huh?

18:07.520 --> 18:09.640
Wh-What is it?

18:11.400 --> 18:13.180
Do you... want this?

18:14.030 --> 18:18.510
Y-Yes... If I can have it.

18:18.510 --> 18:20.200
Okay, here you go.

18:20.200 --> 18:22.280
What was that about?

18:20.200 --> 18:22.520
We'll be going, then.

18:22.280 --> 18:24.330
Does he not want to tear it down?

18:22.520 --> 18:23.720
Bye, now.

18:24.330 --> 18:25.200
I dunno...

18:25.830 --> 18:29.500
I thought he didn't care
about Grandma's café, but...

18:31.460 --> 18:33.680
Looks like you're up now, Ouka.

18:33.680 --> 18:34.590
Huh?

18:35.000 --> 18:37.270
Make that pilaf.

18:41.880 --> 18:45.480
Apparently her son and his wife
died in a car accident.

18:45.480 --> 18:48.120
And she's taking in her grandson
to raise as her own.

18:48.480 --> 18:51.190
Oh, dear... I bet that'll be rough.

18:58.100 --> 19:01.640
It's pilaf for dinner, Master.

19:02.870 --> 19:05.210
Huh? Where's this coming from?

19:05.210 --> 19:07.370
If you made it, I don't want it.

19:07.870 --> 19:12.250
It's the only dish Grandma
taught me how to make.

19:14.600 --> 19:16.700
If you don't want it, just throw it out.

19:18.870 --> 19:20.890
She said it was her grandson's favorite,

19:20.890 --> 19:25.540
so she wanted me to make it for him
if anything happened to her.

19:26.140 --> 19:27.350
Bye.

19:33.570 --> 19:35.500
The old hag's pilaf, huh?

19:37.730 --> 19:38.900
No wonder it looks...

19:39.570 --> 19:41.420
so plebeian.

19:42.560 --> 19:45.500
I'm sorry! I'm truly sorry!

19:46.610 --> 19:50.910
I told you that old people can't run cafés.

19:51.280 --> 19:54.130
Just sell this dumb place already.

19:54.560 --> 19:59.700
I promise I'll repay what I borrowed
from you by next month!

20:04.600 --> 20:06.070
Damn it, what the hell?

20:06.840 --> 20:09.660
Who does she think I got into Tokyo U for?

20:11.240 --> 20:16.310
I was going to show up all those jerks
who looked down on my grandma...

20:16.960 --> 20:17.820
Damn it!

20:19.590 --> 20:23.420
Maybe he's not as cold-hearted as I thought.

20:27.780 --> 20:30.570
Hey, you're doing the dishes for me?

20:30.570 --> 20:32.710
I used them, so I'll clean them.

20:32.710 --> 20:36.220
Oh, you ate it, then? I'm so glad!

20:36.220 --> 20:37.230
How was it?

20:37.230 --> 20:38.710
Normal, I guess.

20:38.710 --> 20:41.460
Huh?! What do you mean, "normal"?!

20:41.460 --> 20:43.080
Can I ask you something?

20:43.080 --> 20:44.000
Huh?

20:44.000 --> 20:46.510
Did my grandma always
eat dinner with you guys

20:46.810 --> 20:50.890
the way we all ate together last night?

20:52.690 --> 20:56.770
Well, yeah. We always ate
and laughed together.

20:57.920 --> 21:00.910
What was she like just before she died, then?

21:00.910 --> 21:01.700
Huh?

21:02.800 --> 21:06.790
She said she was tired from laughing,
so she was going to lie down.

21:06.790 --> 21:09.190
I thought she'd fallen asleep
under the kotatsu,

21:09.810 --> 21:13.910
but when I tried to wake her up... she was...

21:15.040 --> 21:16.220
I see.

21:17.320 --> 21:18.950
I'm glad, then.

21:19.410 --> 21:20.920
Glad?

21:22.340 --> 21:23.990
Because Grandma...

21:24.710 --> 21:27.680
passed away laughing and having fun
with her family, right?

21:33.350 --> 21:36.350
All right! Bring me the
café's account ledgers!

21:36.350 --> 21:37.220
Huh?

21:37.690 --> 21:39.730
Familia Proceeds
2017

21:39.940 --> 21:41.320
Old hag...

21:42.160 --> 21:44.320
These are almost all deficits!

21:44.600 --> 21:47.290
I'm amazed the café didn't go under sooner.

21:47.800 --> 21:52.520
It went over budget because
all five of you were working here!

21:52.520 --> 21:55.610
Wh-What are you getting all testy for?!

21:55.960 --> 21:59.210
What do you expect to get
out of looking at the ledgers now?

21:59.640 --> 22:01.180
I'm going to do it.

22:01.640 --> 22:03.960
I'll run this café in Grandma's place!

22:06.320 --> 22:08.250
Y-You're gonna run the café?!

22:08.250 --> 22:10.970
B-But, Hayato-kun, what about Tokyo U?

22:11.310 --> 22:15.220
I decided to just pay my tuition
and take the year off.

22:15.550 --> 22:17.520
After that, if I don't get results,

22:17.520 --> 22:19.980
I'll turn this place
into a parking lot for real.

22:19.980 --> 22:21.400
Hang on a minute!

22:21.400 --> 22:24.480
Does that mean you'll be living with us?

22:24.480 --> 22:27.800
Well, I mean, this is my house to begin with.

22:27.800 --> 22:29.750
If you don't like it, move out.

22:29.750 --> 22:31.150
You despot!

22:31.150 --> 22:33.990
No kidding. I <i>am</i> the master of this house.

22:34.400 --> 22:37.260
Okay! I'll stay here, then!

22:37.260 --> 22:38.500
Ami-chan?!

22:38.500 --> 22:41.510
Well, moving is just a major pain.

22:43.400 --> 22:46.620
Okay, fine. We can just think of it
as a share house.

22:47.060 --> 22:48.380
I'll stay, too.

22:48.380 --> 22:50.540
Y-You too, Riho-san?

22:50.540 --> 22:51.460
Um...

22:51.890 --> 22:53.310
What about you, Akane-san?

22:53.310 --> 22:54.390
Me?

22:54.960 --> 22:58.630
Not like there's really a choice.
I'm broke, anyway.

22:59.540 --> 23:02.740
Then... I guess I'll stay, too.

23:02.740 --> 23:06.400
With five of us here, we should be okay,
even if there's a guy with us.

23:07.300 --> 23:09.630
Why are you counting me in this?!

23:09.630 --> 23:11.160
S-Sorry!

23:11.500 --> 23:13.910
So what're you gonna do, Ouka-san?

23:16.610 --> 23:19.700
I-I'll stay. What choice do I have?

23:20.570 --> 23:24.170
Will these five be the goddesses of
good fortune who save this café,

23:24.850 --> 23:28.120
or the devils of poverty that sink it?

23:28.670 --> 23:33.820
Either way, I've gotten tangled up
with some real pains in the rear.

23:35.930 --> 23:39.100
We look forward to living with you, Master!

23:41.940 --> 23:56.950
Episode 2: "A Promise with Grandma"

23:42.610 --> 23:45.040
You're the goddesses?
Was the title just a scam?

23:45.040 --> 23:46.680
What should it have been, then?

23:46.680 --> 23:48.780
"It's said that there are devils

23:49.210 --> 23:51.690
living in an old coffee shop
on a beach somewhere."

23:51.690 --> 23:53.080
Welcome...

23:53.080 --> 23:54.450
<i>The Café Terrace
and Its Devils.</i>

23:54.450 --> 23:56.650
No one's gonna watch that!
